# Project Report

## Implementation summary
The project contains a worker process and a controller process. The worker prints its PID and a counter at two-second intervals. The controller launches it and accepts single-character commands from the terminal.

## Test plan
| Test | Action | Expected observation |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Start `./controller` | Controller prints worker PID; worker begins printing |
| 2 | Enter `p` | Worker output pauses |
| 3 | Enter `r` | Worker output resumes |
| 4 | Enter `t` | Controller requests termination; worker exits safely |
| 5 | Start again and press Ctrl+C in the worker terminal context | `SIGINT` handler requests safe exit when delivered to the worker |

